course: dictionary
lesson: 15044
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use the clues around them to find the right one. Read the words next to the tricky word first. Those words are its context.
explain: «Mia is a retiring girl who sits at the back and rarely speaks.» Here retiring describes Mia. The clues sits at the back and rarely speaks tell you it means shy and quiet, not liking to be noticed.
explain: «My grandad is retiring next month.» Now retiring is a verb. He is stopping work because of his age. The clue is next month, and people usually retire from their jobs. Ask: does the word describe a person, or does it tell us what someone is doing? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Retiring can be an adjective, which describes a person, or a form of the verb retire.
fact: As an adjective, «retiring» means shy and quiet, not liking to be noticed.
fact: As a verb, «retiring» means stopping work because of age. In cricket, a batter may also «retire hurt», which means leaving the game early because of an injury.
fact: «Retiring age» is the age at which people stop work.
fact: Retire, retires, retired and retiring are all forms of the same verb.
exercise: «Ben is a retiring boy who likes to read alone at break.» What does retiring mean here? | Very tall | Old and ready to stop work | *Shy and quiet | Loud and funny
exercise: «Nan is retiring from her job at the school next summer.» What does retiring mean here? | Running very fast | Coming back to school | *Stopping work because of age | Being shy in class
exercise: «The batter had to retire hurt after the ball hit his arm.» What does retire mean in this sentence? | *Leave the game early because of an injury | Go to bed early | Score six runs | Start the game
test: «The retiring woman sat quietly in the corner and did not speak to anyone.» What does retiring describe? | A very loud person | A hot day | A person who is leaving work | *A shy person who does not like to be noticed
test: «Dad will be retiring at sixty-five, and then he will get a pension.» What does retiring mean? | Being shy | Going to bed | Leaving the game early | *Stopping work because of age
exam: «The tired king went retiring to his room after the feast.» What does retiring mean here? | Leaving a race early | *Going to bed or to a quiet place to rest | Shy and quiet | Stopping work because of age
